  "turns": [
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hi, it’s good to meet you. What brings you in today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S014",
      "patient_response": "Hi, nice to meet you too. Well, I guess... I mean, the main thing that brings me in is that I just feel like I’m constantly running on a motor lately. I’m a special education teacher, and you know, it’s a job that keeps you on your toes, but this is different. It’s like... I finish one thing at school, say, wrapping up a lesson with my kids or filling out an IEP report, and instead of just taking a breath for a second like a normal person, I immediately jump right into the very next task. I just can't stop moving. \n\nAnd it’s not just at work, either. I get home, and you'd think a guy my age—I'm 58—would want to sit down in his recliner after a long day, but no, I walk in the door, drop my bag, and instantly start cleaning the garage, or pacing around the kitchen, or fixing something out in the yard. I just jump from one thing to the next without ever being able to shut myself off. It’s like the engine is just revving all day long and I don't have the keys to turn it down. My wife says it makes her tired just watching me, and honestly, it's exhausting to live it. I just... I can't seem to stop and just sit still, if that makes any sense?",
