    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Do unwanted thoughts keep popping into your mind even when you try to ignore them?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "No, I wouldn't say I have unwanted thoughts popping in, not like... not like things I'm trying to push away or ignore. It's not that kind of intrusive, bothersome thing where I'm thinking about something terrible or something I don't want to think about. It's more just... well, like I was saying before, it's just the volume and the speed of the thoughts. \n\nIt's like, I'll be sitting there trying to grade a stack of modified math worksheets—and let me tell you, grading for special ed takes a very specific kind of focus because you're not just looking for the right answer, you're looking at the *process* the kid used, trying to figure out where the disconnect happened in their reasoning—but while I'm doing that, my brain is just ping-ponging all over the place. I'm thinking about the math worksheet, yes, but I'm also thinking about whether the tires on my truck need rotating, and then I'm thinking about how I need to call my brother back about his upcoming visit, and then I'm wondering if I remembered to take the chicken out of the freezer for dinner, and then I'm back to the math worksheet, but only for a second before I start thinking about a new behavioral strategy for one of my students who has been acting out during transition times. \n\nIt's just a constant stream of *stuff*. But it's all normal stuff, you know? Everyday things, tasks, plans, ideas. None of it is unwanted or scary or weird. I don't sit there trying to block it out because it's bad, I just get frustrated because there's so much of it all at once and it won't quiet down so I can just do the one thing I'm supposed to be doing. My wife calls it my \"popcorn brain\" because it's just pop, pop, pop, one thought after another. But no, to answer your question, they aren't unwanted thoughts that I'm fighting against. It's just a very crowded, very noisy waiting room up there, and everyone is talking at the same time.",
